# What EAS uploads for the openhome iOS build.
#
# EAS archives the whole GIT REPOSITORY, not the npm workspace. MonoClaw's root
# holds a dozen unrelated projects (travelog 332 MB, projects 198 MB, highfi
# 108 MB, lumen 40 MB, ...), so the archive was 1.2 GB when the build needs
# about 25 MB of it. An earlier attempt put this file in apps/mobile/, which
# EAS never reads — it is only honoured at the archive root, i.e. here.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything, re-admit open-home/, then drop the parts of
# open-home/ the build does not need.

/*
!/open-home/

# Dependencies — EAS runs its own install from package-lock.json (415 MB).
/open-home/node_modules/
/open-home/**/node_modules/

# Enclosure CAD, renders and product mockups (54 MB); never bundled in the app.
/open-home/hardware/

# The TV/display surface and the legacy web app (20 MB) — separate from mobile.
/open-home/apps/app/
/open-home/tv/

# Keep services/cloud and services/hub: they are npm workspaces named in
# package-lock.json, and removing them makes `npm ci` fail on a lockfile
# mismatch. They are only ~1 MB together, so there is nothing to gain anyway.

# Local build artefacts and secrets that must never leave this machine.
/open-home/apps/mobile/creds/
/open-home/apps/mobile/credentials.json
**/*.p12
**/*.mobileprovision
**/.env
**/.env.*
